From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:01:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pan/bi: retrieve the interpolation position for later varying
 loads

Every interpolated varying load is emitted with .store, which recomputes
the interpolation position and writes the hidden varying state, so
va_insert_flow makes it wait for all outstanding varying loads. A
fragment shader reading two varyings serializes them. Within a block,
once a load has stored the centre interpolation position, later centre
loads can use .retrieve: no recompute and no wait.

Only centre interpolation retrieves. A .retrieve load with the centroid
or sample mode faulted the shader core with INSTR_INVALID_ENC on a
Mali-G615 (Pseudoregalia, UE5 through DXVK: the title scene's GPU jobs
fault and the 3D scene is missing), like the fused VAR_TEX encodings,
which have no centroid or sample retrieve either.

The pass runs on the final instruction order, after scheduling, register
allocation and the post-RA cleanups: varying loads carry no ordering
dependencies, so the pre-RA schedulers may move a retrieving load above
the load that stores the position (it then interpolates at a stale
position: Batman: Arkham Asylum's title and menu backgrounds came out as
blocky noise), and DCE may delete the storing load.

On Mali-G615, 32 layers of blended full-screen quads whose shader reads
UV + colour: 2.01 ms -> 1.35 ms (DDK 1.26 ms). Output bit-identical.
BIFROST_MESA_DEBUG=noretrieve disables the pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: stop serializing interpolated varying loads in Valhall fragment shaders
Upstream-commit: none (upstream Mesa also emits .store on every load)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none
Validation test: 2026-10-26: retrieve limited to centre interpolation after Pseudoregalia (UE5, DXVK) faulted the shader core with INSTR_INVALID_ENC on centroid/sample .retrieve loads (bisected to this patch; 0 faults with BIFROST_MESA_DEBUG=noretrieve and with the fix, 2 runs; Arkham title/menu still correct); combined build rg045.so (fcfb64ae4566, rg477m/001-045): PanProbe 38/38 x2; vkd3d-proton 2.14.1 suite 306 -> 309 PASS (test_shader_eval_attribute_dxbc/dxil FAIL -> PASS), none worse; Pseudoregalia 0 GPU faults, title scene renders; Deep Rock Galactic D3D12 title 71 fps; DXVK unchanged: Hades 460 fps, Jupiter Hell tutorial 49.1 fps, Serious Sam D3D11 57.8 fps (uncapped, quietd Stock). Earlier: blended full-screen quads reading UV + colour 2.01 -> 1.35 ms (DDK 1.26), framebuffer checksums identical with and without the pass; PanProbe 38/38. 2026-10-19: pass moved after scheduling/RA; Batman: Arkham Asylum's title and menu backgrounds (blocky noise before, correct on the stock driver and with noretrieve) now render correctly; drawbench fill 32 with UV + colour 1.65 ms (2.50 with noretrieve), drawbench 6 tests' checksums and racetest 5 modes identical to the previous build, PanProbe 38/38
